    "crossref": {
      "source": "crossref",
      "found": true,
      "raw": {},
      "title": "ELIXIR-UK DaSH: A Fellowship of data stewards",
      "abstract": "<ns3:p>\n                  In 2021, ELIXIR-UK was granted a UKRI award for the\n                  <ns3:ext-link xmlns:ns4=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" ext-link-type=\"uri\" ns4:href=\"https://elixiruknode.org/about/projects/data-stewardship-training-project/\">ELIXIR-UK DaSH Fellowship</ns3:ext-link>\n                  . The University of Bradford leads the project, along with a delivery team at Cardiff University, the Earlham Institute, the University of Manchester and the University of Oxford.\n                </ns3:p>\n                <ns3:p/>\n                <ns3:p>The project aims to produce and deliver training in FAIR data stewardship and Research Data Management (RDM), using ELIXIR-UK knowledge and resources, such as the RDMkit and the FAIR Cookbook.</ns3:p>\n                <ns3:p/>\n                <ns3:p>It focuses on building capacity and professionalising Data Stewardship while leveraging the local expertise of diverse UK universities and research institutes \u2013 creating a data management culture from within the institutions.</ns3:p>\n                <ns3:p/>\n                <ns3:p>\n                  The project is looking to recruit a total of 20 Data Steward Fellows, who will act as RDM and FAIR ambassadors. The first cohort of nine experienced Fellows has already been meticulously selected to start working on:\n                  <ns3:list list-type=\"order\">\n                    <ns3:list-item>\n                      <ns3:p>Creating short training videos \u2013 RDMbites</ns3:p>\n                    </ns3:list-item>\n                    <ns3:list-item>\n                      <ns3:p>Develop open RDM online courses catered for life science researchers</ns3:p>\n                    </ns3:list-item>\n                    <ns3:list-item>\n                      <ns3:p>Deliver RDM courses at their respective institutions to build capacity</ns3:p>\n                    </ns3:list-item>\n                  </ns3:list>\n                  The leading and delivery teams of the grant will simultaneously focus on building a community of practice, overseeing and coordinating the training curriculum, and ensuring the sustainability of the Fellowship beyond the project.\n                </ns3:p>",
